    T56
        title       Durability: release versions, key fingerprints and record migration (slice 2b)
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T21]
        satisfies   [@plan.Persistence.O5, @plan.Runtime.O3]
        description
            Build release versions on production: key fingerprints, identity versions, saved-shape resets with record 
            migration, and `previous` holds checked against Restore R6 (slice 2b).

            **Why now:** an upgraded release must reset or keep each saved record correctly. Split from @task.V3.T20 
            (orchestrator, 2026-11-12, wide consult W3) because a saved shape is defined only once @task.V3.T17 and 
            @task.V3.T57 fix private and computed fields and fragments, and identity versions need @task.V3.T9's 
            value-named actors; built before them it would be built on Pay-shaped machines and rebuilt.

            **Read first:** @spec.Restore, @spec.Codec, @task.V3.T20 (the restore it extends), 
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/fable-wide-consult-2026-11-12.md (W3, item 2).

            Absorbs @task.V3.T26 (record migration, @plan.Persistence.O5; real storage shapes are IndexedDB structured 
            clone from @task.V3.T58) and @task.V3.T11's migration wrong runtimes. Codes: up pg. Part built: S25 [A]. 
            Bench: the S25 upgrade boot. Blocked by @task.V3.T21 for the slice order (W3, item 4).

            **Phase-out, step 5 (the user accepted 2026-11-11):** the Stamp twin (release 1 and 2 keys; `up`) is 
            written in `fixtures/`; run the hand cases on it on production; write production mutants per oracle the 
            slice judges, mapped by Invariant from the round-14 mutants; delete `stamp.ts` once the derived reference 
            equals it. Read code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/conformance-phase-out-2026-11-11.md.

            - **May change:** `src/`, the conformance fixtures, model and generator.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.

            False pass: a reset judged from the runtime's report, not the bytes → caught by the restore oracle and the 
            Stamp twin's round-14 verdicts.
            Gates: the suite; falsify; the matrix and combination gates; `nub run check`.
            Stops: a guarantee change.
        acceptance
            The Restore area passes on production in full, with every Restore Invariant's oracle or case killing its 
            mutants.
            - Record migration passes cases on production: a changed saved shape resets its definition's records with 
              the writes in flight kept (from @task.V3.T26, @plan.Persistence.O5).
            - Key fingerprints, identity versions and `previous: [{ key }]` holds pass cases on production (Restore R6).
            - The slice's generated runs pass on production, and its benchmark replay matches the work fingerprint.
            - Declared: up pg are in the production and Spec-model capability lists, and the feature-matrix gate shows 
              none of them as owed.
            - Enabled: S25 [A] and the parts built earlier declare those codes among their needs, the generator draws 
              their operations, and the app mix runs them.
            - Covered: the combination gate counts the pairs among implemented codes, fails an unexercised interacting 
              pair with no dated waiver, and passes before this Task closes.
            - Guards: production's first-contact reds are recorded and classified, held-out seeds pass, and a sample of 
              the model's expectations is read by a different model family (Fable).
            - Phase-out step 5: the Stamp twin exists in `fixtures/` and `stamp.ts` is deleted; the same verdict per 
              case on round-14 and production.
            - Phase-out checks (the four validations): no lost catch in the catch matrix; the same coverage and 
              feature-matrix rows; the derived reference equal to the hand rows wherever both exist; Compile static 
              cases green on each fixture's `Compiled`.
